      "problem": "What's the domain of $y={log}_{5}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{5}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14257461/assets/f095d09fd04a982ad51ff3859f6d789083ed7528b382457954e45cf259cc06a5.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{5}⁡x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x>0.$",
